      "rule": "R10",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "For `CREATE TABLE t(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,c INT CHECK(c>0),w INT) STRICT; INSERT INTO t VALUES(1,1,0),(2,1,0); UPDATE t SET id=1,w='x' WHERE id=2;`, the model reports the type failure of `t.w`, but SQLite 3.51.0 skips the unaffected CHECK and reports `UNIQUE constraint failed: t.id`. Fix: account for which CHECK constraints the UPDATE evaluates when ordering late type failures, and add this regression case."
